Id: sctl003w
Severity: WARN
Category: kernel
Check: check_sysctl
Fix: Set vfs.usermount=0 in /etc/sysctl.conf.
References: sysctl.conf(5); sysctl(8); mount(8)
Controls: CIS 4.1, 10.5; NIST CM-6, SI-16; ISO 8.9; CE Secure configuration

vfs.usermount is 1, so any user may mount file systems: a removable
disk or image with a setuid-root binary on it, which then runs as
root, or a filesystem crafted to confuse the kernel. FreeBSD lets
only root mount unless told otherwise:
  # sysctl -w vfs.usermount=0
and keep it in /etc/sysctl.conf.
